module std where

-- FM-retire-9 Step 9c / FM-retire-11 — the three bodied class-A combinator
-- residuals (`bindResult`, then `.` and `$`) are authored here, leaving std.ts
-- at `defineFunction` floor 0.
--
-- 9c moved `bindResult` (matrix-neutral — unsampled). `.` and `$` STAYED TS at
-- floor 2 through FM-retire-10 because a naïve `.fenel` port REGRESSED their
-- JS+Wasm self-host: the parser strips the `{var}` wrapper off a lowercase
-- application head (→ a bare-string head), and the self-host chokepoint
-- `normalise-to-core:resolveCallee` lowers a bare-string head as a GLOBAL
-- reference (`$fenel.f(x)`), not the captured local — so the compiled `std:$`
-- threw `$fenel.f is not a function`. The retired TS bodies dodged this by
-- hand-writing `{var:"f"}` heads.
--
-- FM-retire-11 (Decision C(a) = GO L1) removes that blocker at the SOURCE: a
-- post-parse scope-resolution pass in the loader (`resolveLocalCallHeads`,
-- fenel-module.ts) rewrites a local-applying bare-string head back to `{var}`
-- BEFORE registration. So the bodies below — `(.) f g = \x -> f (g x)` and
-- `($) f x = f x` — carry `{var}` heads by the time any consumer sees them, the
-- compiled core IR is byte-identical to the retired TS bodies' (`{var}`→`$dyn:`
-- via resolveCallee), and `.`/`$` self-host on JS + Wasm exactly as before. The
-- L1 pass also retired the 9c `callOp` interpreter band-aid (json-logic.ts):
-- the head arrives `{var}` from the loader now, so the interpreter resolves it
-- through the normal `{var}` path.
--
-- Documented, accepted divergences from the retired TS specs (both already ride
-- the module-migrate-std oracle's normalizations): type-params load as `{$ref}`
-- not the TS `{$var}` (parseTypeAtom; folded by the oracle); and the `.fenel`
-- facet vocabulary has no `@example` directive — the TS specs' `examples` are
-- dropped (no Δ to the oracle, which never stored examples).

-- bindResult — Result-monad bind (Kleisli composition). Lets composite decoders
-- short-circuit on the first Err instead of nesting `case … of Err … -> Err …`
-- at every step. Substrate for the typed Update decoder + its record-tier
-- siblings (Phase 11c sub-step 2c).
@label "Bind Result (>>=)"
@description "Result-monad bind / Kleisli arrow chaining. `bindResult r f` returns Err e unchanged when r is Err, otherwise applies f to the Ok value. Lets composite computations short-circuit at the first failure without nesting case-of at each step. ∀e a b. Result e a → (a → Result e b) → Result e b."
@tags "function" "combinator" "result" "monad"
bindResult : (r: Result e a) -> (f: (a -> Result e b)) -> Result e b
bindResult r f =
  case r of
    Err _e -> Err _e
    Ok _x -> f _x

-- (.) — function composition. (f . g)(x) = f (g x). The body's `f`/`g`
-- application heads parse as bare strings; the L1 loader pass rewrites them to
-- `{var}` heads (they name the params f/g), so the compiled core IR matches the
-- retired TS body and JS+Wasm self-host is preserved.
@label "Compose (.)"
@description "Function composition operator: (f . g)(x) = f(g(x)). Infix alias for `compose`. ∀a b c. (b → c) → (a → b) → (a → c)"
@tags "function" "combinator" "operator" "higher-order"
@category "function"
(.) : (b -> c) -> (a -> b) -> (a -> c)
(.) f g = \x -> f (g x)

-- ($) — low-precedence function application. `f $ x` = `f x`. The application
-- head `f` rewrites to a `{var}` head via the L1 loader pass (it names the
-- param f).
@label "Apply ($)"
@description "Function application as a low-precedence right-assoc operator. f $ x = f x. ∀a b. (a → b) → a → b"
@tags "function" "combinator" "operator"
@category "function"
($) : (a -> b) -> a -> b
($) f x = f x
